granted below.

1. Definitions.

   "The licensed materials" means the copyright holder's own work in this repository
   and in the separately archived offline kit that the release notes name by digest:
   the manuscript, the companions, the figures, the proof bundle's proofs, statements,
   pins, records, logs, oracles, verifier sources and build drivers, the referee trail
   as reproduced here, and the front matter. It excludes the third-party material
   identified in section 4 or listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

   "Non-commercial" means not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial
   advantage or monetary compensation. Use inside a company or under a grant is
   non-commercial when the use itself is research, teaching, verification or private
   study and the licensed materials are not offered, embedded or relied upon in a
   product, service or offering.

   "Research group or class" means the members of one research group, project team or
   taught class working or studying together, and their collaborators on that work.

   "Published results" means descriptions, measurements, comparisons, conclusions,
   independent reimplementations written without copying the licensed materials, and
   outputs obtained by running the licensed materials (such as verification results,
   decoded statements and scores), including quotations under section 2(d), but not the
   licensed materials themselves or modified versions of them, and not weights or
   models derived from the bundled models.

2. Permitted uses. Subject to section 3, you may, without charge and solely for
   non-commercial purposes:
   (a) view, download and keep copies of the licensed materials for private study;
   (b) verify the proofs, run the verifier, decode the statements, rebuild the programs
       and study how the materials work;
   (c) use, copy, run and modify the licensed materials, other than LICENSE and
       CITATION.cff, for research and teaching, and share copies, including modified
       copies, within a research group or class for that work; and publish the results
       of that work with attribution;
   (d) quote reasonable excerpts with attribution.
   Attribution means naming the author, the title, the version and the repository
   recorded in CITATION.cff.

3. Reserved rights. Everything not granted in section 2 is reserved. In particular,
   without the prior written permission of the copyright holder you may not:
   (a) use the licensed materials, or anything derived from them, for a commercial
       purpose;
   (b) redistribute the licensed materials, modified versions of them, or substantial
       parts of them, outside a research group or class, other than the quotations that
       section 2(d) allows; publishing results is permitted, redistributing the materials
       is not;
   (c) distribute weights or models derived from the bundled models;
   (d) sublicense any of the licensed materials;
   (e) use the names ZeeBeam, Dark Lantern, Truth Beam, PolieBotics or BOSUN, or the
       copyright holder's name, to endorse or promote derived work;
   (f) remove or alter this licence, the copyright notice, CITATION.cff or
       THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

4. Third-party materials. The frozen source tree includes a modified copy of the
   jubjub crate, licensed by its authors under MIT or Apache-2.0 at your option; the
   three guest ELFs incorporate target-runtime code from packages named in the frozen
   guest-workspace Cargo.lock files and Rust standard-library components; build
   dependencies and procedural macros run during compilation and are not target-linked;
   the applicable packages and licences are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, with the
   licence texts in licenses/; the vendored crates in the
   offline kit belong to their authors under the licences recorded in the kit's own
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md; the toolchain archives carry their own licences;
   figures/zeebeam.svg embeds DejaVu Sans glyph outlines under the Bitstream Vera licence
   and figures/zeebeam.png renders them; the three PDFs embed DejaVu subsets under that
   licence, and paper/zeebeam.pdf also embeds a Liberation Serif subset under the SIL Open
   Font License 1.1; and the fetched
   public data (drand rounds, and the Zcash block and transaction as returned by the
   Blockchair API) is subject to its sources' terms. Those terms govern those materials;
   this licence does not.

5. Patents and trade marks. No trade mark rights are granted. No patent licence is
   granted, except that the copyright holder will not assert patent claims against the
